<title>NETHERLANDS: WHAT'S ON - CONCERTS/THEATRE/OPERA/SHOWS.</title>
<headline>WHAT'S ON - CONCERTS/THEATRE/OPERA/SHOWS.</headline>
<text>
<p>Following are some highlights of cultural events:</p>
<p>				  **CONCERTS**</p>
<p>				  ============</p>
<p>ROCK/POP...</p>
<p>APR 21    -- Suede, Vredenburg, Utrecht</p>
<p>APR 23    -- Kenny G, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 1-2   -- Supertramp, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 6-8   -- Peter Andre, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 7     -- Alan Parsons, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 11    -- The Who perform 'Quadrophenia', Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 16-17 -- Tony Braxton, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 27    -- Aerosmith, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>MAY 27    -- Marco Borsato, Carre, A'dam</p>
<p>MAY 30    -- Jean-Michel Jarre, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>JUN 1     -- Bryan Adams, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>JUN 7-8   -- Diana Ross, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>JUN 8     -- Michael Jackson, Amsterdam ArenA</p>
<p>JUN 9     -- BoyzOne, Vredenburg, Utrecht</p>
<p>JUN 15-16 -- Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds, RAI, A'dam</p>
<p>JUN 18    -- Celine Dion, Amsterdam ArenA</p>
<p>JUL 18-19 -- U2, Feyenoord Stadion, R'dam</p>
<p>OCT 1     -- Supertramp, Ahoy, R'dam</p>
<p>Tickets available through Ticketlijn:  0900-3001250</p>
<p>CLASSICAL..</p>
<p>APR 15    -- Amsterdam Baroque Orchestra and Choir</p>
<p>		 Concertgebouw, A'dam, 020-6718345</p>
<p>OPERA......</p>
<p>APR 30    -- Luciano Pavarotti, Amsterdam ArenA</p>
<p>Tickets available through AUBuitlijn, 020-6211211</p>
<p>				 **THEATRE**</p>
<p>				 ===========</p>
<p>AUG 20    -- Joe (A Musical Production), Carre, Amsterdam</p>
<p>020-4212223</p>
<p>				 **CIRCUS**</p>
<p>				 ==========</p>
<p>TO APR 20 -- Alegria -- Canadian circus troupe Cirque du</p>
<p>Soleil's latest extravaganza.</p>
<p>Tickets available through Alegria Ticketlijn, 020-6862109</p>
<p>				 **MUSEUMS**</p>
<p>				 ===========</p>
<p>TO MAY 19 -- History of Andres Serrano/History of Sex -- Work by</p>
<p>controversial American photographer.</p>
<p>Groninger Museum, Museumeiland 1, Groningen, 050-3666555</p>
<p>TO MAY 25 -- Ulrich Ruckriem -- The Stedelijk Museum had to</p>
<p>reinforce its floors to support some of the 24 massive</p>
<p>sculptures by this German artist. </p>
<p>Stedelijk Museum, Paulus Potterstraat 13, A'dam, 020-5732911</p>
<p>TO JUNE 8 -- The Early Mondriaan -- An exhibition of the</p>
<p>artist's paintings and drawings up to 1920 illustrating his</p>
<p>development and motivations for his image-less style. </p>
<p>Kunsthal Westzeedijk 341, Rotterdam, 010-4400300</p>
<p>TO SEPT 14-- Rarely seen works of Italian masters from</p>
<p>middle-ages featuring works done in gold-leaf.  </p>
<p>Rijksmuseum, A'dam, 020-6732121</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
